WEBVTT

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:03.730
Shark and the thugs are going to steal cards?

00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:06.150
You should stay away from Shark!

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:07.400
You’re wrong!

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:09.150
This isn’t just for Shark!

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:12.280
This battle is also for me!

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:14.030
I’ll win this duel!

00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:17.490
And I’ll make Shark come to his senses!

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:18.540
Be careful, Yuma.

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:20.700
There’s something strange about this duel.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:22.660
Be quiet!

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:26.040
Here I go! I’m kattobing!

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:32.590
Your monster is destroyed,
and you take damage equal to its ATK.

00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:37.970
That’s the power of Volcasaurus’s Mag Max!

00:00:39.890 --> 00:00:41.220
Yuma...

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:43.310
This is bad.

00:00:43.310 --> 00:00:47.690
But Volcasaurus used all of its Overlay Units.

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:51.400
It can’t use its Mag Max effect anymore.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:52.570
You’re right!

00:00:52.570 --> 00:00:55.150
All right! The battle is just getting started!

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:57.530
Just getting started?

00:00:57.530 --> 00:00:59.780
Ryoga, you’re going down first.

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:06.120
Volcasaurus attacks you directly with 2500 ATK, Ryoga!

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:10.840
Shark!

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:13.260
I activate my trap!

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:16.550
Zeus’s Breath!

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:21.760
Your monster’s attack is negated.

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:24.730
He had that set card ready.

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:27.900
That saved us.

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:29.560
Saved you?

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:31.980
Your fields are empty.

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:34.190
We’ll finish you next turn.

00:01:34.190 --> 00:01:37.660
I set two cards and end my turn!

00:01:38.870 --> 00:01:41.120
My turn! I draw!

00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:45.410
I summon Goblindbergh!

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:53.800
When this card is summoned, I can Special Summon one Level 4-or-below monster from my hand!

00:01:56.220 --> 00:02:00.090
I Special Summon Level 4 Gagaga Magician!

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:02.100
Two Level 4 monsters!

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:03.560
Wait, Yuma!

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:05.770
I’m kattobing!

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:10.810
I overlay Level 4 Gagaga Magician and Goblindbergh!

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:14.530
With these two monsters, I build the Overlay Network!

00:02:14.530 --> 00:02:16.240
Xyz Summon!

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:21.620
Appear, Number 39!

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:25.790
Utopia!

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.000
Hooray! It’s Utopia!

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:33.630
Why?

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:36.960
Yuma is relying on his Number.

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:41.090
The Number appeared.

00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:42.680
That’s what we were waiting for.

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:45.850
I activate the Continuous Trap Avalanche!

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:54.320
When this card activates,
the Xyz Monster you summoned can’t attack!

00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:56.030
Utopia!

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:02.200
Utopia is frozen!

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:09.910
And if the Xyz Monster uses its effect,
you take 500 points of damage.

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:11.000
Oh no!

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:13.210
That means I can’t use Utopia’s effect!

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:16.050
A trap specifically for Xyz Monsters.

00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:18.010
That summoning was pointless.

00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:21.720
I set two cards and end my turn!

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:24.430
As long as we seal away his Number, we’ll win.

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:26.430
Let’s finish them quickly.

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:29.230
My turn! I draw!

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:31.310
Change battle position!

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:34.230
Icebergdon switches to attack position!

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:35.820
I’ll finish you, Ryoga!

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:41.030
Icebergdon attacks Ryoga directly!

00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:42.950
Die!

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:47.790
I activate Utopia’s effect!

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:50.660
It negates a monster’s attack!

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:51.960
You fool!

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:55.460
Did you forget about the Continuous Trap Avalanche’s effect?

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:58.250
You’ll take 500 points of damage!

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:01.920
I said that we’re friends!

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:05.800
Moon Barrier!

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:10.850
Take Avalanche’s effect!

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:24.740
Whether it’s rain, wind, blizzard or the scorching sun

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:27.870
They give color to each day
Will and love keep me from losing heart

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:30.450
Your kindness was harsh
I learned frustration when we clashed

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:34.670
Freedom begins by accepting differences Dance and create the universe

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:42.420
In truth, I was sad until I met you

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:48.720
I lied, thinking it was easier to be alone

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:55.100
Even though we don’t like the same books or hobbies

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:59.020
You’re the only one who agreed with me

00:04:59.020 --> 00:05:01.820
Joy and sadness and anger and do re mi fa so la ti do

00:05:01.820 --> 00:05:03.570
There’s no harmony and scenario without differences

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:07.620
Everyone is not the same

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:11.700
That’s the reason for living

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:17.880
Even if the sounds are dissonant at times

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:22.920
That’s why I never give up
I believe my strength will get me through

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:26.550
I travel to the edge of the world

00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:31.010
The sights I see with you are the truth

00:05:31.010 --> 00:05:33.850
Whether it’s rain, wind, blizzard or the scorching sun

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:37.100
They give color to each day
Will and love keep me from losing heart

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:40.060
Your kindness was harsh
I learned frustration when we clashed

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:44.150
Freedom begins by accepting differences Dance and create the universe

00:05:48.030 --> 00:05:49.660
Yuma!

00:05:53.290 --> 00:05:58.000
\hUtopic Combo! Armored Xyz Activates!\h

00:05:53.290 --> 00:05:58.000
Number 12:

00:05:53.290 --> 00:05:58.000
Did Yuma summon Utopia in order to protect Shark?

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:00.500
I didn’t need him to do that.

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:02.670
What beautiful friendship.

00:06:02.670 --> 00:06:05.760
You made a good friend.

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:08.050
I’ll strike you again!

00:06:08.050 --> 00:06:12.720
Pompadour Blizzardon attacks Ryoga directly!

00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:16.730
I activate Utopia’s effect!

00:06:16.730 --> 00:06:19.020
Moon Barrier!

00:06:28.910 --> 00:06:30.820
Yuma...

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:33.530
Damn...

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:34.790
What’s wrong?

00:06:34.790 --> 00:06:37.500
You can keep laying down if you want.

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:40.540
Be quiet!

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:42.250
I was just taking a rest!

00:06:42.750 --> 00:06:44.960
The battle is only getting started!

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:47.420
You still don’t understand.

00:06:47.420 --> 00:06:49.630
They don’t know our power.

00:06:49.630 --> 00:06:53.390
I activate the trap Volcanic Ash!

00:06:53.390 --> 00:06:59.440
This card’s effect switches Kaio’s monster Pompadour Blizzardon to defense position!

00:07:00.190 --> 00:07:03.560
Why would he switch his teammate’s monster to defense position?

00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:05.780
You did it, bro!

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:12.410
Thanks to that, I can activate the spell card Frozen Ice Cave!

00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:17.750
A monster on my field in defense position gains 1 Level.

00:07:17.750 --> 00:07:19.080
What?

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:23.830
I increase Pompadour Blizzardon from Level 4 to 5!

00:07:23.830 --> 00:07:26.550
Two Level 5 monsters!

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:32.840
I overlay Level 5 Icebergdon and Pompadour Blizzardon!

00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:37.350
With these two monsters,
I build the Overlay Network!

00:07:37.350 --> 00:07:39.600
Xyz Summon!

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:52.530
Appear, Number 19: Freezerdon!

00:07:57.700 --> 00:07:59.830
A second Number!

00:07:59.830 --> 00:08:02.830
I activate Freezerdon’s effect!

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:11.590
By using one Overlay Unit, my teammate’s Xyz Monster regains all Overlay Units!

00:08:11.590 --> 00:08:12.840
What?

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:15.550
Regains its Overlay Units?

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:26.900
Since it regained Overlay Units, it can use Mag Max again!

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:28.440
Those guys...

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:31.650
I set two cards and end my turn.

00:08:33.150 --> 00:08:37.160
No one can beat us in a tag duel!

00:08:37.160 --> 00:08:39.870
There’s something strange about this duel.

00:08:40.410 --> 00:08:41.790
They’re cheating.

00:08:42.250 --> 00:08:43.540
Cheating?

00:08:43.960 --> 00:08:47.000
What are you talking about?

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:50.590
Don’t play dumb! You’re cheating!

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:54.130
What’s this “somewhat” you’re talking about?

00:08:54.130 --> 00:08:57.090
“Cheating!” It means to be unfair!

00:08:57.090 --> 00:08:58.350
Unfair?

00:08:58.760 --> 00:09:01.350
They’re being dishonest in this duel?

00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:04.390
That’s what cheapskates would do.

00:09:04.390 --> 00:09:10.070
They memorized the order
of the cards in each other’s decks.

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:14.700
They also messed with their Duel
Disks’ auto-shuffle systems.

00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:21.790
I see! That’s why they both happened to have Level 5 monsters in their hands.

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:26.870
When they used trap cards to switch their teammate’s monster to defense position...

00:09:26.870 --> 00:09:31.920
...and used spell cards to increase their monsters’ Levels in order to Xyz Summon...

00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:37.590
...it’s because they knew what cards were in each others’ hands and what they would draw next.

00:09:37.590 --> 00:09:41.310
If that’s the case, they’re not duelists!

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:45.770
Real duelists never cheat!

00:09:45.770 --> 00:09:49.110
Cheating? You’re one to talk!

00:09:49.610 --> 00:09:52.360
You’re the cheater.

00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:54.940
You cheated during the national tournament!

00:09:57.990 --> 00:10:00.490
You’re no contender.

00:10:00.490 --> 00:10:04.500
You peeked at your opponent’s deck in the waiting room during the finals!

00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:11.090
It’s time for the Duel Monsters
National Tournament Finals.

00:10:11.090 --> 00:10:14.960
Contender Ryoga Kamishiro has advanced easily.

00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:18.880
I must win.

00:10:19.930 --> 00:10:23.180
What duel will they show us?

00:10:27.100 --> 00:10:29.270
His deck?

00:10:30.060 --> 00:10:37.490
Ryoga! Ryoga!

00:10:37.490 --> 00:10:39.950
It’s the climax of the final duel!

00:10:40.530 --> 00:10:41.910
Neither duelist has backed off!

00:10:41.910 --> 00:10:44.990
I can win. Just a little more.

00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:49.290
He sets one card and ends his turn!

00:10:49.290 --> 00:10:51.830
A set card... Can it be?

00:10:51.830 --> 00:10:55.840
“Mirror Force”

00:10:51.830 --> 00:10:55.840
He would play that card in this situation.

00:10:55.840 --> 00:10:57.720
I can win!

00:10:58.510 --> 00:11:00.130
My turn! I draw-

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:06.020
Ryoga Kamishiro is disqualified
from this duel due to cheating.

00:11:06.560 --> 00:11:11.480
Kamishiro cheated by looking
at his opponent’s deck.

00:11:11.480 --> 00:11:17.190
Due to that incident, you got a lifetime ban
from dueling’s main stage.

00:11:19.570 --> 00:11:22.910
I was afraid of losing.

00:11:25.030 --> 00:11:28.700
A contender is afraid of losing!

00:11:28.700 --> 00:11:30.710
How lame!

00:11:30.710 --> 00:11:32.630
He’s pathetic.

00:11:34.750 --> 00:11:36.800
Stop laughing!

00:11:37.630 --> 00:11:39.550
What’s so funny?

00:11:39.550 --> 00:11:42.890
What’s so funny about being afraid of losing?

00:11:42.890 --> 00:11:44.720
I was also scared.

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:48.180
When I thought that I would lose,
I suddenly became scared.

00:11:48.180 --> 00:11:51.020
That’s why I used a Number!

00:11:51.850 --> 00:11:57.110
I said that I did it to rescue Shark,
but it was because I was afraid to lose!

00:11:57.110 --> 00:11:58.940
I lied!

00:11:58.940 --> 00:12:00.360
Yuma...

00:12:01.740 --> 00:12:07.660
That’s why when it comes
to dueling, I’ll never lie again!

00:12:07.660 --> 00:12:10.200
I know Shark feels the same.

00:12:10.200 --> 00:12:13.080
That’s why Shark’s dueling is real!

00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:18.090
Even if you cheat, we’ll
fight fair-and-square and win!

00:12:18.710 --> 00:12:21.050
That’s how we now duel!

00:12:21.510 --> 00:12:23.430
You’re all talk.

00:12:23.430 --> 00:12:27.220
You only have a frozen Number on your fields.

00:12:27.220 --> 00:12:29.270
What can you do with that?

00:12:29.890 --> 00:12:31.180
Yuma.

00:12:31.850 --> 00:12:34.140
Let’s win this duel.

00:12:35.850 --> 00:12:37.860
My turn! I draw!

00:12:37.860 --> 00:12:42.320
I activate the spell card Xyz Gift from my hand!

00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:47.780
When there are two or more Xyz Monsters on the field, I draw two cards.

00:12:47.780 --> 00:12:50.200
I summon Needle Sunfish!

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:57.170
Then I activate the spell card Surface from my hand!

00:12:57.170 --> 00:13:02.840
I Special Summon one WATER monster from my graveyard in face-up defense position!

00:13:02.840 --> 00:13:05.180
Appear, Big Jaws!

00:13:06.140 --> 00:13:07.340
This is...

00:13:07.340 --> 00:13:10.850
I overlay Level 3 Needle Sunfish and Big Jaws!

00:13:11.270 --> 00:13:14.810
With these two monsters, I build the Overlay Network!

00:13:14.810 --> 00:13:16.520
Xyz Summon!

00:13:16.520 --> 00:13:19.520
Appear, Black Ray Lancer!

00:13:19.520 --> 00:13:21.110
Black Ray Lancer!

00:13:21.110 --> 00:13:24.190
I activate Black Ray Lancer’s effect!

00:13:24.190 --> 00:13:31.080
I use one Overlay Unit to negate Volcasaurus’s effect until the End Phase!

00:13:31.080 --> 00:13:32.240
What?

00:13:32.240 --> 00:13:34.460
Now we can destroy his Number!

00:13:34.460 --> 00:13:38.080
But Volcasaurus has higher ATK!

00:13:38.080 --> 00:13:39.630
Not good enough, Rikuo!

00:13:39.630 --> 00:13:41.170
I activate Needle Sunfish’s effect!

00:13:41.170 --> 00:13:47.840
Since this card was sent to the graveyard, Volcasaurus loses 500 ATK!

00:13:47.840 --> 00:13:49.350
2000 ATK!

00:13:49.720 --> 00:13:52.560
Black Ray Lancer has higher ATK!

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:55.350
He turned the tables.

00:13:55.350 --> 00:13:59.310
Black Ray Lancer attacks Volcasaurus!

00:13:59.310 --> 00:14:01.570
Go! Black Spear!

00:14:03.570 --> 00:14:06.700
I activate the trap Compensation Exchange!

00:14:06.700 --> 00:14:09.280
This card negates the battle.

00:14:09.820 --> 00:14:13.740
In exchange, I take damage equal to Volcasaurus’s ATK!

00:14:13.740 --> 00:14:16.210
He took its place?

00:14:16.210 --> 00:14:18.540
I attack while Kaio defends.

00:14:18.540 --> 00:14:21.420
That’s how we fight!

00:14:21.420 --> 00:14:22.380
I activate my trap!

00:14:22.380 --> 00:14:24.380
Volcanic Abyss!

00:14:24.380 --> 00:14:32.300
When a teammate takes effect damage, I can look at your hand. If there’s a monster card, it returns to your deck.

00:14:32.300 --> 00:14:34.890
I’ll look at your hand!

00:14:35.270 --> 00:14:36.770
My hand?

00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:40.810
He’s trying to stop you from summoning a monster next turn.

00:14:41.230 --> 00:14:43.270
My cards!

00:14:44.860 --> 00:14:47.780
Gogogo Golem and Monster Reborn.

00:14:47.780 --> 00:14:49.740
Monster Reborn.

00:14:49.740 --> 00:14:52.410
He’s not capable of mastering that card.

00:14:52.410 --> 00:14:55.790
Return the monster card to your deck!

00:14:56.660 --> 00:14:58.750
Gogogo Golem...

00:15:00.710 --> 00:15:03.710
I set one card and end my turn.

00:15:03.710 --> 00:15:05.960
Now you’re done!

00:15:05.960 --> 00:15:07.880
My turn! I draw!

00:15:08.340 --> 00:15:10.430
Ryoga, you’re first!

00:15:10.880 --> 00:15:13.680
I activate Volcasaurus’s effect!

00:15:13.680 --> 00:15:18.640
One of your monsters is destroyed, and you take damage equal to its ATK.

00:15:18.640 --> 00:15:20.600
I destroy Black Ray Lancer!

00:15:20.600 --> 00:15:25.110
Ryoga takes damage equal to its ATK
for 2100 points of damage!

00:15:26.150 --> 00:15:27.650
Shark!

00:15:27.650 --> 00:15:32.030
Take Mag Max!

00:15:37.790 --> 00:15:40.290
Take this, Ryoga!

00:15:41.370 --> 00:15:42.880
I activate my trap!

00:15:43.580 --> 00:15:45.420
Damage Diet!

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:49.050
Effect damage is halved this turn!

00:15:53.300 --> 00:15:56.010
Due to Volcasaurus, my trap activates!

00:15:56.470 --> 00:15:58.220
Icy Crevasse!

00:16:00.060 --> 00:16:08.900
When a card effect destroys my monster, your monster is destroyed, and you take damage equal to its ATK!

00:16:08.900 --> 00:16:11.240
You’re aiming for mutual destruction!

00:16:11.240 --> 00:16:12.360
I activate my trap!

00:16:12.860 --> 00:16:14.320
Forced Change!

00:16:14.320 --> 00:16:17.830
I switch the trap’s target to Freezerdon!

00:16:25.670 --> 00:16:27.920
Kaio!

00:16:29.130 --> 00:16:31.590
All right! We defeated Kaio!

00:16:31.590 --> 00:16:34.050
How dare you defeat my younger brother!

00:16:34.050 --> 00:16:37.180
You won’t leave unscathed!

00:16:37.180 --> 00:16:39.310
I activate Volcasaurus’s effect!

00:16:39.720 --> 00:16:40.720
I destroy Utopia!

00:16:41.180 --> 00:16:44.900
Take Mag Max!

00:16:48.020 --> 00:16:49.730
Utopia!

00:16:50.780 --> 00:16:53.200
Damage Diet!

00:16:53.200 --> 00:16:54.950
How rude!

00:16:54.950 --> 00:16:57.780
Volcasaurus attacks Ryoga directly!

00:16:58.160 --> 00:17:00.740
I activate the trap Final Offering!

00:17:02.040 --> 00:17:09.630
This card ends the battle, and I give one card in my hand to another player.

00:17:09.630 --> 00:17:10.460
Yuma!

00:17:11.380 --> 00:17:12.420
Me?

00:17:12.420 --> 00:17:14.220
I can be the other player?

00:17:14.630 --> 00:17:15.680
Yeah.

00:17:15.680 --> 00:17:17.180
That card is...

00:17:17.180 --> 00:17:18.970
Give up already!

00:17:18.970 --> 00:17:22.640
I activate the Continuous Spell Twin Volcano!

00:17:22.640 --> 00:17:27.350
This card deals 500 points of damage during each of my Standby Phases.

00:17:27.770 --> 00:17:32.610
I can also send this card to the graveyard to deal 500 points of damage!

00:17:32.610 --> 00:17:33.820
That means...

00:17:33.820 --> 00:17:38.740
When it’s his turn again, you will both have 0 LP.

00:17:38.740 --> 00:17:41.080
Now we’ll win!

00:17:42.240 --> 00:17:44.710
Prepare yourselves!

00:17:44.710 --> 00:17:46.210
Don’t give up.

00:17:46.710 --> 00:17:48.670
We can still win.

00:17:50.090 --> 00:17:52.420
My turn! I draw!

00:17:54.090 --> 00:17:56.550
We can still win?

00:17:56.550 --> 00:17:59.550
You should be able to figure it out.

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:03.390
Can you figure out what he’s thinking?

00:18:03.390 --> 00:18:08.770
All I can do is use Monster Reborn
to bring back Utopia...

00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:11.110
Armored Xyz!

00:18:11.520 --> 00:18:13.730
Shark gave me this card.

00:18:13.730 --> 00:18:14.530
I see!

00:18:14.990 --> 00:18:19.740
Monster Reborn can also resurrect a monster from the opponent’s graveyard.

00:18:19.740 --> 00:18:25.290
I activate the spell card
Monster Reborn from my hand!

00:18:25.290 --> 00:18:27.460
He’s going to Special Summon Utopia!

00:18:27.460 --> 00:18:31.920
I Special Summon Black Ray Lancer
from Shark’s graveyard!

00:18:36.170 --> 00:18:39.300
Why? Black Ray Lancer has less ATK!

00:18:39.300 --> 00:18:40.640
You’re an amateur!

00:18:40.640 --> 00:18:42.050
Oh really?

00:18:42.050 --> 00:18:42.800
What?

00:18:42.800 --> 00:18:47.810
I activate the spell card Armored Xyz from my hand!

00:18:47.810 --> 00:18:49.440
Armored Xyz?

00:18:49.440 --> 00:18:52.770
I gave him a card that’s specifically for Xyz Monsters.

00:18:52.770 --> 00:18:59.400
An Xyz Monster in my graveyard equips onto a monster on my field!

00:18:59.820 --> 00:19:02.030
Appear, Utopia!

00:19:03.410 --> 00:19:06.950
I equip Utopia onto Black Ray Lancer!

00:19:18.970 --> 00:19:25.220
Even though it has 2500 ATK, did you forget that only a Number can destroy a Number?

00:19:25.220 --> 00:19:26.720
But it can be destroyed.

00:19:26.720 --> 00:19:27.520
What?

00:19:27.520 --> 00:19:32.020
Due to Armored Xyz,
Black Ray Lancer’s name becomes Utopia’s.

00:19:32.020 --> 00:19:35.150
In other words, it becomes a pseudo Number!

00:19:35.150 --> 00:19:37.190
Pseudo Number?

00:19:37.190 --> 00:19:38.860
That means Volcasaurus will be...

00:19:38.860 --> 00:19:41.360
Go, Black Ray Lancer!

00:19:41.360 --> 00:19:43.410
Attack Volcasaurus!

00:19:53.250 --> 00:19:57.630
Then due to Armored Xyz,
by sending Utopia to the graveyard...

00:19:57.630 --> 00:20:01.220
...Black Ray Lancer can attack again!

00:20:01.220 --> 00:20:04.180
I send Utopia to the graveyard!

00:20:04.970 --> 00:20:06.890
Go, Black Ray Lancer!

00:20:06.890 --> 00:20:08.930
Attack Rikuo directly!

00:20:09.270 --> 00:20:10.890
Unbelievable!

00:20:11.730 --> 00:20:14.400
Black Spear!

00:20:25.530 --> 00:20:26.740
They won!

00:20:26.740 --> 00:20:28.410
You did it, Yuma!

00:20:28.410 --> 00:20:31.330
Observation #12:

00:20:31.330 --> 00:20:34.250
This is how you two duel.

00:21:00.070 --> 00:21:01.940
What happened to us?

00:21:01.940 --> 00:21:04.780
Why did we want to steal cards?

00:21:07.870 --> 00:21:09.740
Shark!

00:21:09.740 --> 00:21:11.330
Run away!

00:21:11.330 --> 00:21:12.700
What’s up with them?

00:21:12.700 --> 00:21:14.960
Never come back!

00:21:17.420 --> 00:21:19.000
Tetsuo...

00:21:19.880 --> 00:21:21.090
I’m sorry!

00:21:21.090 --> 00:21:22.880
I lied to you!

00:21:22.880 --> 00:21:24.010
Forgive me!

00:21:24.970 --> 00:21:26.550
Umm...

00:21:30.890 --> 00:21:32.770
It’s fine.

00:21:32.770 --> 00:21:35.020
Why don’t we duel instead?

00:21:35.020 --> 00:21:36.770
Nice!

00:21:36.770 --> 00:21:37.730
Right now?

00:21:38.940 --> 00:21:40.230
Shark!

00:21:41.070 --> 00:21:42.940
Umm...

00:21:42.940 --> 00:21:44.190
Oh yeah!

00:21:44.190 --> 00:21:47.160
I’ll give Armored Xyz back.

00:21:47.160 --> 00:21:49.240
You can have that card.

00:21:49.830 --> 00:21:53.620
It seems the amateur duelist
has improved his skills a bit.

00:21:54.540 --> 00:21:56.080
Amateur?

00:21:57.830 --> 00:21:59.290
See ya.

00:22:04.670 --> 00:22:06.170
Shark...

00:22:13.180 --> 00:22:15.810
Let’s start the duel!

00:22:16.560 --> 00:22:18.560
This week’s quiz:

00:22:18.560 --> 00:22:24.530
Do you activate a trap card
from your hand? Or after you set it?

00:22:30.070 --> 00:22:34.790
Today’s test is hard
Can’t avoid pleasure and temptation

00:22:34.790 --> 00:22:39.920
I want to go home and watch TV
Recent cartoons are entertaining

00:22:49.840 --> 00:22:54.390
Anyway, tests are hard
Language, math and English are especially hard

00:22:54.390 --> 00:22:59.520
Average scores in science and social studies
I’m only good at P.E.

00:22:59.520 --> 00:23:01.940
(Wait, Baby!) The expected

00:23:01.940 --> 00:23:04.570
(What’s that, Baby!) Answers

00:23:04.570 --> 00:23:06.940
(Wait a sec, Baby!) Remember them

00:23:06.940 --> 00:23:08.860
(What are we!? Baby!) For who

00:23:08.860 --> 00:23:13.530
Let’s say I wrote the correct answers on that sheet

00:23:13.530 --> 00:23:18.080
Will that change the future a year or a decade from now?

00:23:18.120 --> 00:23:23.460
The world I drew at the edge of dreams

00:23:23.460 --> 00:23:28.130
Someday I’ll race in the sky

00:23:28.130 --> 00:23:33.260
Nobody can threaten my heart

00:23:33.260 --> 00:23:37.060
Nothing is correct!

00:23:40.890 --> 00:23:43.440
Someone else is gathering Numbers?

00:23:44.270 --> 00:23:46.900
I’ll defeat him in a duel!

00:23:46.900 --> 00:23:49.320
What? Time has stopped?

00:23:49.320 --> 00:23:51.660
You’re the Number Hunter!

00:23:51.660 --> 00:23:54.160
Yuma, he’s dangerous! Run away!

00:23:54.570 --> 00:23:58.580
He’s stronger than anyone you or I have ever faced!

00:23:58.580 --> 00:24:02.000
That makes me want to battle even more!

00:24:02.000 --> 00:24:09.970
\h\hThe Soul Hunter! The Number Hunter Appears!\h\h

00:24:02.420 --> 00:24:08.050
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZEXAL:
“Hunter of Souls! The Number Hunter Appears!”

00:24:08.050 --> 00:24:09.970
I’m kattobing!

00:24:12.680 --> 00:24:13.970
The answer is...

00:24:14.550 --> 00:24:16.550
After you set it!

00:24:16.550 --> 00:24:20.140
You have to prepare in order to unleash a trap.

00:24:20.140 --> 00:24:24.480
You must set it before activating it.
